1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,896
Cryptography hides in source, dependencies, configuration, certificates and container images.

2
00:00:04,896 --> 00:00:09,242
CryptoDrishti finds all of it — and turns it into one inventory you can defend.

3
00:00:11,092 --> 00:00:20,949
One scan: 23 distinct assets, 16 quantum-vulnerable — and the scan's own completeness stated up front.

4
00:00:23,192 --> 00:00:27,830
Five RSA findings in one scan. A signing call goes to ML-DSA-65.

5
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:32,468
RSA wrapping a key is key establishment — a hybrid key exchange, a completely different migration.

6
00:00:32,468 --> 00:00:37,106
And a cipher list that never says what RSA is for gets no target at all.

7
00:00:37,106 --> 00:00:41,744
Purpose decides the migration.

8
00:00:43,594 --> 00:00:48,005
A key deleted by a later container layer is still reported — it is still extractable.

9
00:00:48,005 --> 00:00:52,416
And a refused endpoint makes the scan PARTIAL, and it says why.

10
00:00:55,694 --> 00:01:02,960
The output is a CycloneDX bill of materials, validated offline against the official JSON Schema.

11
00:01:07,794 --> 00:01:13,293
CryptoDrishti · Team Zero-Day · SIH26164
